  "title": "Accepted numeric Inclusive tax mode is persisted raw and consumed as Exclusive",
  "evidence_chain": [
    "TaxMode declares Inclusive first (underlying0). Create36/Update88 Enum.TryParse result is discarded, accepted Mode string stored unchanged42/98. Request Mode is a string, not a typed canonical enum.",
    "Checkout63, Cashier126 and CallCenter150 interpret only literal Inclusive as inclusive and every other stored string as Exclusive. All three share the same lossy projection, so cross-client agreement would not establish correct input interpretation.",
    "A legitimate settings_manage request Mode=\"0\", positive tax rate and Enabledtrue parses a defined Inclusive value but stores0; selected active rule then applies exclusive tax to later checkout and client estimates. One selected active rule assumed to avoid unrelated multiple-enabled ambiguity.",
    "Illustrative source arithmetic only: base10000piastres at1400basispoints should remain total10000 under Inclusive, but Exclusive yields11400. No TaxEngine/API/DB execution performed for this candidate."
  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Valid authenticated settings_manage actor, new valid config request or update, positive rate, chosen enabled rule subsequently selected and normal valid sale.",
    "A noncanonical numeric-string configuration value is supplied. Current shipped settings UI may only send canonical names; ordinary UI trigger not claimed."
  ],
  "counterevidence": [
    "TryParse here is case-sensitive; lowercaseinclusive is rejected. Do not claim ignoreCase on this handler.",
    "Canonical Inclusive/Exclusive work; numeric1 maps Exclusive consistently; rate0 masks economic difference.",
    "Configuration authority can intentionally change taxes; this is accepted-input interpretation/canonicalization defect, not unauthorized tax change or tax-law guidance.",
    "Existing orders store frozen tax figures; update affects future selection, not automatic rewrite of historical records."
  ],
  "recommended_solution": "Validate explicit defined mode policy, either reject numeric/noncanonical strings or persist parsedMode.ToString and consume with one explicit parser that rejects unknown state. Do not silently default unsupported modes to Exclusive.",
  "regression_risks": "Changing only one client mapping leaves server and other client divergence. Preserve named modes, optional disabled rule, valid zero rate, historical frozen tax and idempotent config replay.",
  "required_tests": [
    "Defined numeric0 versus namedInclusive, numeric1 versusExclusive, undefinednumeric2, whitespace and wrongcase according to explicit policy.",
    "Selected enabled config across bothclientestimates/server checkout yields same intendedTaxMode; reject unsupported mode before any write.",
    "Normal namedInclusive/Exclusive, disabled/zero-rate controls and historical-order tax invariants."
  ],
  "independent_verification": "Original specialist has source-clarified defined numeric issue in message; formal artifact requested before canonical promotion.",
